\ times ( xt n -- ) — run xt n times. No arity contract on the xt.

\ basic: print '*' five times
[: 42 emit :] 5 times cr

\ zero count: quotation never runs
[: "boom" . :] 0 times

\ quotation that leaves values: data stack grows each iter
[: 7 :] 3 times .s clear cr

\ each-side-effect ordering: 0 1 2 3 4 printed in order. The running value lives
\ on the stack, not in a local — a quotation cannot write the word's frame
: count-up  0  [: dup . 1 + :] 5 times  drop ;
count-up cr

\ wrong types
[: :] -1 times
"x" [: :] times
5 5 times

clear
\ i-times ( xt n -- ) — run xt n times, pushing the index 0..n-1 before each call.

\ basic: print 0 1 2 3 4
[: . :] 5 i-times cr

\ zero count: never runs
[: "boom" . :] 0 i-times

\ index is the only thing pushed; quotation that ignores it leaves it
[: drop :] 3 i-times .s clear cr

\ sum of 0..9 via a stack accumulator under i-times: 45
: sum-up-to  0 swap  [: + :] swap i-times ;
10 sum-up-to . cr

\ sum of squares 0..4: 0+1+4+9+16 = 30
: sum-sq  0 swap  [: dup * + :] swap i-times ;
5 sum-sq . cr

\ a receiving quotation whose body under-produces drives the data stack empty:
\ the loop-refill underflow is caught, not a buffer overflow (ASan-verified)
clear
1 [> a | :] 3 times
clear
1 [| a >b | :] 3 times

\ wrong types
[: drop :] -1 i-times
"x" [: drop :] i-times
5 5 i-times

clear
\ === fold-times ( acc map-xt combine-xt n -- acc' ) ===
\ the map body is ( i -- term ); the combiner never sees the data stack when it
\ is a primitive arithmetic word, so the accumulator stays in the combinator

\ sum of 0..4 with the identity map, and sum of squares 0..4
0 [: :] ' f+ 5 fold-times . cr            \ 10
0 [: dup f* :] ' f+ 5 fold-times . cr     \ 30

\ product of 1..5, and subtraction to show the combiner's operand order
1 [: f1+ :] ' f* 5 fold-times . cr        \ 120
100 [: :] ' f- 5 fold-times . cr          \ 90 — acc combines on the left

\ zero count answers the initial accumulator untouched
:untouched [: :] ' f+ 0 fold-times . cr   \ :untouched

\ a quotation combiner takes the dispatched path and sees ( acc term -- acc' )
0 [: :] [: f+ :] 5 fold-times . cr        \ 10
[ ] [: :] [: add-last! :] 3 fold-times . cr   \ [ 0 1 2 ] — combiner sees ( acc term )

\ a parked value is read by depth; here f* consumes the index, so the body needs
\ no cleanup
7 0 [: 1 pick f* :] ' f+ 4 fold-times nip . cr   \ 42 — 7·(0+1+2+3)

\ the wrappers: sum-times and product-times supply the defaults
[: :] 5 sum-times . cr                    \ 10
[: dup f* :] 4 sum-times . cr             \ 14
[: f1+ :] 5 product-times . cr            \ 120

\ wrong types
0 [: :] ' f+ -1 fold-times
0 [: :] 5 fold-times
0 5 ' f+ 5 fold-times
